We study the McKean--Vlasov free energy on the unit sphere associated with the unnormalized self-attention (USA) model for noisy transformer dynamics. We prove a sharp global-minimizer dichotomy in every dimension $d\ge2$. There is a unique $β_*^{(d)}&gt;0$ such that \begin{equation*}
 \frac{I_{d/2+1}(β_*^{(d)})}{I_{d/2}(β_*^{(d)})}=\frac1d, \end{equation*} where $I_ν$ is the modified Bessel function of the first kind. For $0&lt;β\le β_*^{(d)}$, the uniform density remains the unique global minimizer up to the linear-stability threshold \begin{equation*}
